// Occlusion by the train's own walls (spec A.5 "car walls -12 dB and lowpass at 900 Hz", A.7 "occlusion via raycast against
// car geometry"; ARCHITECTURE §8 note 248). Every positioned sound but the train's bed is heard through the walls between
// it and the ear: the line from one to the other is tested against each car's interior. A wall it crosses is a whole
// wall (mix.json occlusionDb and occlusionLowpass), unless it crosses where a door, the roof hatch or a breach is open.
{
  // A wall of a car with something open in it lets this much of a wall through: the sound comes round by the door.
  "openWall": 0.6,
  // An opening's leaf, made this much bigger each way (m): what's at its edge comes round it.
  "openingMargin": 0.15,
  // A breach's hole (spec B.9, Vehicle.BreachAt): within this of it (m), a sound goes through it, not the wall.
  "breachRadius": 0.9,
  // In a stop's building (ARCHITECTURE §8 note 396; the "shed" and "room" spaces, note 392), what's outside it comes through
  // its walls: a shed's or the hero's bays stand open (a little of a wall), a room's one door is broken open (most of one).
  "shedWall": 0.35,
  "roomWall": 0.8,
  // And what's in one comes out through the same walls to an ear outside it (note 428), unless it's within this of the
  // building's face on the ear's side (m): at its door or a window, heard out of it.
  "roomEdge": 0.5
}
